      "Description": {
        "Scope of Services": "The Empire Migrant Housing Complex, located at 5132 South Avenue, Empire, CA. 95319, is seasonal and only operational for the timeframe of November through March for cold weather shelter, and the Family Housing Facility, located at 1128 South 9th Street, Modesto, CA. 95354, allows families to gain much-needed stability, sufficient time to engage in services and continue their permanent housing search with case management support. CSA, along with partners, will be working closely with these families to help them obtain the services and support necessary by utilizing wraparound services and whole-family support, including employment services. The future service provider shall hire one (1) property manager at each location to live on site and to provide property management services. Services are further described in Exhibit A-1 Scope of Work and Exhibit A-2 Scope of Work.\n\nEach proposal must cover services for both properties listed above. Proposers must submit one (1) proposal for both the Empire Migrant Housing Complex and the Family Housing Facility. Although both sites are included under one solicitation, there will be two (2) separate contracts – one (1) for each property. Therefore, please provide two (2) pricing proposals and budget narratives, one for each location.\n\nThe successful Proposer must meet all the requirements and expectations set forth herein, as well as all the general contractual and insurance requirements mandated by the County (“Terms and Conditions). Terms and conditions may be modified through the RFP process.\n\nProposers must thoroughly explain how their Proposal meets or exceeds the service and deliverable expectations specified in the RFP.",
